      "verdict": "accept_bounded_whole_DEEN_source_witness",
      "scientificReason": "The restricted pure KBr/KCl alternatives, matched reference observations and blank support the KBr assignment. Ag+ + Br− → AgBr(s) conserves Ag, Br and total charge zero. Cream/pale-yellow AgBr versus white AgCl is consistent with the independently read RSC method. Appropriate dilute HNO3 limits carbonate interference while adding no chloride. The fresh HCl scenario adds its own Cl−, so precipitation cannot establish originally present chloride. The fresh unknown mixture correctly prevents inference of exclusive Br−, pure KBr or a bromide mass fraction. No ammonia dissolution subtest is obligatory for the expressly binary controlled written case.",
      "controlsAndLimits": "Blank, same-condition KBr positive and KCl discrimination reference are supplied; other silver-precipitating species and intrinsic color are excluded only within the original binary model. K+ derives from the candidate set, not silver precipitation.",
      "wholeTaskModelAlignment": "DE and EN both demand selection of the supplied sequence, charge-balanced interpretation, counterion/amount boundaries and the distinct reagent-contamination transfer. Neither language asserts laboratory execution.",
      "operatorPerformance": "Selection and written interpretation of supplied controlled observations; no individual practical execution evidence.",
      "hold": false
    },
    {
      "caseLocalKey": "bbbe-carbonate-acid-gas-controlled-intention-author-v4",
      "wholeCaseSha256": "8451890f92a1e050001fce5472240c5a8085720e8c09688a5899f101f8c03a94",
      "verdict": "accept_bounded_whole_DEEN_source_witness",
      "scientificReason": "Within pure Na2CO3/NaCl alternatives, controlled acid-driven gas evolution and separate positive CO2/limewater observation support carbonate. CO3²− + 2 H3O+ → CO2 + 3 H2O conserves atoms and charge zero. CO2 + Ca(OH)2 → CaCO3(s) + H2O explains precipitation. HCO3− + H3O+ → CO2 + 2 H2O has the same gas signature, so expanding the candidates removes unique carbonate identification. CaCO3 + CO2 + H2O → Ca²+ + 2 HCO3− balances atoms and charge zero; later clearing does not erase the documented initial cloud.",
      "controlsAndLimits": "NaCl and reagent blanks, carbonate positive and CO2 reference separate gas production from gas identity. Hydrogencarbonates, sulfites and other gas-formers are excluded only in the original choice. Bubbles alone identify neither gas nor amount; Na+ and salt-mixture pairing are not measured.",
      "wholeTaskModelAlignment": "Whole DE/EN material, task, model and fresh excess-CO2 transfer match. Proton acceptance and the separate gas assay are both explained. The retained 580 gas profile is supporting chemistry only and supplies no operative current BB/BE source role.",
      "operatorPerformance": "Written selection/design interpretation, no experiment performed by a learner.",
      "hold": false
    },
    {
      "caseLocalKey": "bbbe-ammonium-hydroxide-basic-gas-controlled-intention-author-v4",
