      "verdict": "accept_bounded_whole_DEEN_source_witness",
      "scientificReason": "Given NH4Cl/NaCl alternatives and controlled exclusions, hydroxide treatment with controlled warming releases NH3 from NH4+. NH4+ + OH− → NH3 + H2O conserves atoms and charge zero. NH3 + H2O ⇌ NH4+ + OH− explains alkaline response in the water film on damp paper. Neutral gas NH3 is distinguished from NH4+ in solution. Direct NaOH contact is correctly rejected as ammonium evidence. Pre-existing NH3 or another basic gas can explain the fresh unrestricted positive result, so repetition is not unique NH4+ identification.",
      "controlsAndLimits": "Separate damp paper, exclusion of alkaline liquid contact/droplets, reagent and NaCl blanks, ammonium positive and ammonia reference address the actual alternative explanations. Chloride and NH4+ amount are not independently measured.",
      "wholeTaskModelAlignment": "DE/EN preserve the same fictional controlled school context, balanced proton reaction and transfer limits. The learner is not asked to smell ammonia or perform an unsupervised heated test. Held 9dee has no BB/BE applicability and is excluded.",
